{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01R6kLRFPcnZYYai5G4tfXnn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A single-user personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), with plain-markdown files as the source of truth (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files) â€” no database, no sync, no external dependencies beyond Python stdlib (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals).\n\n- **It ships `anchor_gui.py` as its primary interface** â€” a self-contained stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reading and writing the markdown directly. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor`. A CLI engine (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core productivity function:** capture and manage tasks through a full lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored), organized across domains (academic, commercial, family, writing), with quick-capture inbox, priorities, energy levels, due dates, and notes â€” all editable from the browser and logged to daily activity logs.\n\n- **It has grown a substantial \"R&D Control Surface\"** layered on top â€” a mission-control cockpit for \"trio-driven\" R&D work (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). Each project gets a window with per-lane tiles (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass), status lights, and inline expandable panels carrying cached summaries plus real interactive terminals.\n\n- **The terminal substrate is real ConPTY** (via `pywinpty`, the one waived native dependency), with per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini), and xterm.js consoles over a hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE transport. Sessions auto-load the lane's skill once and greet once.\n\n- **It is self-verifying:** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM, fully stubbing all model/PTY calls, exercising every endpoint and the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces, and writes dated reports â€” surfacing a red dashboard banner on any failure.\n\n- **Current state:** the v4 \"Project Cockpit\" redesign is built (9 waves, 637 tests passing) and merged to master; the system is branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear.\"\n\nTwo framings worth noting: the CLAUDE.md describes Anchor as a **personal task/project manager**, while the locked North Stars in the planning docs focus almost entirely on the **R&D cockpit** â€” so the project has effectively become *both* a GTD-style task system and a multi-agent development mission-control, sharing one server and one markdown store."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9de7656a-fb65-4fb3-a9e4-07c392354218","uuid":"5eb87c64-1adc-4c89-b2b6-32aa6bcecfc4","request_id":"req_011Cc1huJEuC76ovMatUAk4v"}
